Implement user story SKY-004-c: Integration tests for Express server endpoints

## Story Description
Create src/server.test.ts using vitest + supertest with SkyscannerClient mocked. At least 8 tests covering all endpoint scenarios: health, root, search (valid/missing params/invalid adults), cheapest (valid/empty/missing params), RAPIDAPI_KEY gating, and client error handling.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/server.test.ts uses vitest + supertest with SkyscannerClient fully mocked (vi.mock or equivalent) — zero real HTTP calls during vitest run
- Test: GET /health returns 200 with JSON body { status: 'ok', uptime: <positive number> }
- Test: GET /health returns 200 even when RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is absent
- Test: GET / returns 200 with Content-Type text/html and body matching src/public/index.html contents
- Test: GET /search with valid params returns 200 with { flights: FlightResult[], count, searchedAt } where count === flights.length
- Test: GET /search missing required param returns 400; non-numeric adults param returns 400; absent adults defaults to 1 and returns 200
- Test: GET /cheapest returns 200 with cheapest FlightResult; returns 404 when client returns empty array; missing param returns 400
- Test: RAPIDAPI_KEY absent → /search and /cheapest return 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; SkyscannerClient throws → endpoint returns 500 { error: string }, no unhandled rejection; `vitest run` exits 0 with all tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- GET /health returns 200 with JSON body { status: 'ok', uptime: <number> }
- GET /health is never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY check - always returns 200
- GET / returns 200 with Content-Type text/html and body from fs.readFileSync on path.join(__dirname, 'public', 'index.html')
- GET /search query params are named 'from', 'to', 'date' - not 'origin'/'destination'
- GET /search missing required param (from/to/date) returns 400 with { error: 'from, to, and date are required' }
- GET /search adults param parsing: undefined defaults to 1; empty string returns 400 { error: 'adults must be numeric' }; non-numeric returns 400 { error: 'adults must be numeric' }
- GET /search when hasKey is false (RAPIDAPI_KEY absent) returns 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }
- GET /search successful response: 200 with { flights: FlightResult[], count: flights.length, searchedAt: new Date().toISOString() }
- GET /search SkyscannerClient is instantiated with new SkyscannerClient() - no apiKey option passed, uses env var
- GET /search SkyscannerClient.searchFlights receives { origin: String(from), destination: String(to), date: String(date), adults: <parsed number> }
- GET /search catch block returns 500 { error: <err.message or 'Internal server error'> }
- GET /cheapest query params are named 'from', 'to', 'date'
- GET /cheapest missing required param returns 400 { error: 'from, to, and date are required' }
- GET /cheapest adults param parsing identical to /search
- GET /cheapest when hasKey is false returns 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }
- GET /cheapest when flights.length === 0 returns 404 { error: 'No flights found' }
- GET /cheapest successful response: 200 with single FlightResult object (cheapest by price comparison using flights.reduce)
- GET /cheapest catch block returns 500 { error: <err.message or 'Internal server error'> }
- hasKey is computed once at module load: const hasKey = !!process.env.RAPIDAPI_KEY
- FlightResult interface: { price: number, currency: string, airline: string, departure: string, arrival: string, duration: number, stops: number }
- app.listen is guarded by if (require.main === module) - supertest will not trigger port binding

## Mock Strategy
Use vi.mock('./skyscanner/client', () => ({ SkyscannerClient: vi.fn() })) with vi.hoisted to hoist the mock, then mock the prototype searchFlights method; in beforeEach use vi.clearAllMocks() to reset call counts between tests

